 ## Overview
-SnugBox is a precise algorithm for computing Gaussian-to-tile bounding box intersections in 3D Gaussian Splatting, replacing the overly conservative tile assignment of standard 3D-GS to reduce the number of pixels processed per Gaussian [S1][S2, unofficial]. It computes a tight axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) around each Gaussian's elliptical extent in image space, assigning the Gaussian only to tiles that strictly intersect this box [S1][S2, unofficial]. Unlike the standard method which inscribes a circle and uses a square bounding box, SnugBox derives the box directly from the conic equation of the projected Gaussian, providing numerical stability under edge-on tilts [S3, unofficial]. It serves as a lossless optimization that reduces the number of Gaussian-tile pairs, contributing to an average inference speed-up of 1.82× [S1].
+SnugBox is a precise algorithm for computing Gaussian-to-tile bounding box intersections in 3D Gaussian Splatting, replacing the overly conservative tile assignment of standard 3D-GS to reduce the number of pixels processed per Gaussian [S1][S2, unofficial]. It computes a tight axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) around each Gaussian's elliptical extent in image space, assigning the Gaussian only to tiles that strictly intersect this box [S1][S2, unofficial]. Unlike the standard method which inscribes a circle and uses a square bounding box, SnugBox derives the box directly from the conic equation of the projected Gaussian, providing numerical stability under edge-on tilts [S3, unofficial]. It serves as a lossless optimization that reduces the number of Gaussian-tile pairs, contributing to an average inference speed-up of 1.82× [S1]. Nearest alternatives include [Warp-Level Culling](12278-warp-level-culling-for-efficient-blending-in-3d-gaussian-spl.md) and [TileSkipper](19190-tileskipper.md).
 
