 ### [Compact Box (CB)](17690-compact-box-cb.md)
-Compact Box (CB) is a preprocessing optimization for rasterization that reduces the number of Gaussian-tile pairs by tightening the effective support region of 2D Gaussians, eliminating unnecessary pairs where the Gaussian has negligible impact on pixels within a tile. It builds on SnugBox by introducing a scaling factor $\beta$ into the alpha blending equation, which further shrinks the 2D Gaussian footprint and intersection region with tiles compared to standard 3-sigma or precise tile-intersection methods.
+Compact Box (CB) is a preprocessing optimization that tightens the effective support region of 2D Gaussians to eliminate negligible tile intersections. It sets itself apart from SnugBox by introducing a scaling factor $\beta$ into the alpha blending equation, further shrinking the footprint. Choose it when maximum tile culling is required at the cost of modified blending weights. [Compact Box (CB)](17690-compact-box-cb.md)
 
